* POSITIVE — 7 trading days
* POSITIVE — 10 trading days

RET_MOM × MARKET_SPY_TREND10

* POSITIVE — 7 trading days
* POSITIVE — 10 trading days

The two RET_MOM × MARKET_SPY_TREND10 cases are prospectively flagged:

LIMITED_TEMPORAL_CAPACITY

because B5A established approximately 46 and 43 eligible trading dates respectively.

Do not remove that flag based on outcomes.

SAMPLE RULE

Use the entire objectively available B5A source envelope.

For each case, use every causally eligible date satisfying its frozen predictor requirements and complete forward horizon while requiring the endpoint to remain strictly before 2025-02-03.

No discretionary date or symbol removal.

No outcome-driven exclusions.

FROZEN CAUSAL SEMANTICS

Preserve the certified causal definitions and all prior frozen semantics.

These include, where applicable:

* adjusted close_t;
* reported daily volume_t;
* RET_MOM = close_t / close_(t-10) - 1;
* finite same-date cross-sectional average_rank / N;
* centered rank = 2 × percentile_rank - 1;
* SPY TREND10 state using the frozen B4/B5 definition;
* state normalization from strictly earlier finite observations;
* minimum 20 prior observations;
* sample SD ddof=1;
* SD > 1e-12.

Use only information causally available at each decision date.

PRIMARY INFERENCE UNIT

Trading date is the primary inference unit.

Do not treat individual symbol/date observations as independent inferential observations.

Construct the frozen date-level cross-sectional effect for each eligible trading date and perform primary inference on the resulting date-level series.

OVERLAPPING-RETURN INFERENCE

Use Bartlett/Newey-West HAC covariance.

For horizon H:

HAC lag = H - 1 trading dates.

Use:

* two-sided inference;
* asymptotic-normal reference distribution;
* 95% confidence interval;
* no unplanned small-sample multiplier;
* sample SD ddof=1 where required.

Report the frozen directional interpretation separately from the two-sided inferential calculation.

Do not convert the primary test into an unplanned one-sided test.

MULTIPLICITY

All nine primary cases form ONE multiple-testing family.

Apply Benjamini-Hochberg jointly across all nine primary p-values.

Primary FDR threshold:

q <= 0.05

Do not split the family by factor, horizon or result.

Unavailable primary cases remain explicitly unavailable and must not silently disappear in a manner that reduces multiplicity burden.

REQUIRED PRIMARY STATISTICS

For every case report at minimum:

* family;
* horizon;
* frozen direction;
* eligible date count;
* mean date-level effect;
* median date-level effect;
* sample SD;
* standardized effect = mean / sample SD;
* HAC standard error;
* 95% HAC CI;
* raw two-sided p-value;
* BH-adjusted p-value;
* positive/negative date share as applicable;
* LIMITED_TEMPORAL_CAPACITY flag.

MATERIAL-EFFECT GATE

Preserve the existing S2 material-effect convention already frozen upstream.

Do not create a more permissive B5-specific threshold.

The exact inherited threshold/convention must be located in authoritative prior frozen decisions and included explicitly in the B5 implementation/manifest before outcome execution.

If the authoritative inherited material-effect rule cannot be determined unambiguously without inspecting B5 outcomes:

STOP BEFORE OUTCOME COMPUTATION.

Return BLOCKED_USER to Indicator: Swing Trades identifying the ambiguity.

Do not invent a threshold.

TEMPORAL STABILITY

Before outcome inspection, deterministically partition each case’s eligible validation dates chronologically into four approximately equal blocks.

Report per block:

* start/end;
* N;
* mean;
* median;
* sign.

Preserve any applicable previously frozen stability gate semantics. Do not remove a poor block.

SYMBOL CONCENTRATION

Where additive symbol contribution is defined, report:

* every symbol’s contribution;
* top-1 absolute contribution share;
* top-5;
* top-10;
* concentration/HHI diagnostic;
* leave-top-five aggregate effect;
* sign reversal after removing top five.

Do not remove symbols from the primary test based on these diagnostics.

MECHANICAL DISPOSITIONS

Exactly one disposition per frozen hypothesis:

INDEPENDENT_VALIDATION_SUPPORTED

PARTIAL_VALIDATION_EVIDENCE

INDEPENDENT_VALIDATION_FAILED

NOT_TESTABLE

INDEPENDENT_VALIDATION_SUPPORTED requires:

* frozen hypothesized sign;
* inherited material-effect gate;
* BH-FDR q <= 0.05;
* required frozen stability gate;
* required concentration gate;
* no semantic/data-integrity failure.

PARTIAL_VALIDATION_EVIDENCE indicates supportive evidence with one or more preregistered confirmation gates failing. It is not equivalent to independent validation.

INDEPENDENT_VALIDATION_FAILED indicates failure of required directional/material/inferential confirmation or substantive contradictory evidence.

NOT_TESTABLE is reserved for a prospectively required estimand that cannot validly be computed because of semantic/data/numerical insufficiency.

The LIMITED_TEMPORAL_CAPACITY flag remains attached to the two market-state tests regardless of mechanical disposition.

NO VALIDATION-SAMPLE RECYCLING

After B5 outcomes are exposed, this validation dataset is used.

Do not use its outcomes to create or confirm:

* new thresholds;
* alternate horizons;
* new factors;
* alternate transformations;
* revised market-state definitions;
* symbol filters;
* date filters;
* new interactions;
* optimized parameters.

Diagnostics may explain results but may not convert an exploratory revision into a validated result on this sample.

Any materially revised hypothesis requires another genuinely untouched sample.

